{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nA store write that cannot acquire the write lock in its budget is DISCARDED — no retry, no spool.\n`acquire()` computes `total_wait = timeout * attempts` into **one** deadline\n(`_store/lock.py:695-698`), so `attempts` is a silent multiplier, not a retry loop. Both legs\nnon-blocking-poll with jitter (`lock.py:215`, `lock.py:628`), so there is no fairness.\n\nRe-measured 2026-08-11 against an APFS clone of the live 737M tracker (numbers in the AC#1\ncomment): the 6-writer storm no longer loses writes (6/6, 16/16, 48/48 all succeed — 7084's\nhold-duration fixes were real), but loss is still terminal and is now driven by HOLDER DURATION.\nA 70s holder + 3 comments → 3/3 exit 1 with **0 of 3 markers present afterwards**. A 45s holder +\none `rebar claim` → fails at exactly **30.30s** (`attempts=1`). A 40s holder left 6 comments\nsucceeding at **59.5s of a 60s budget**.\n\nConfirmed twice more since: the live Jira DC CI run recorded here, and this ticket's own\nplan-review PASS — whose sidecar and attestation were BOTH destroyed by a 60s timeout behind a\n163s holder (comment \"the gate lost its own PASS\").\n\n## Approach\n\n**Bounded retry-with-backoff, not fair queueing.** When one holder outlives the whole budget every\nwaiter fails regardless of service order, so FIFO buys nothing against the measured failure.\nBounded re-attempts convert loss into latency with less machinery than a queue.\n\nRetry is safe without the phantom-write semantics that got R6 (spool-and-adopt) declined on 7084,\nbecause **the retry lives strictly inside `acquire()`**: it re-attempts only the acquisition, and\n`LockTimeout` is raised before the caller's write body runs. Once `acquire()` returns the loop is\nfinished and cannot re-enter, so no write is replayed. A retry at any layer above the lock WOULD\nrisk a duplicate append; that boundary is asserted by test, not merely claimed.\n\nChecked against the \"error surfaced but the write had landed\" shape: one `transition` takes up to\nsix acquisitions, five AFTER the STATUS commit (signature `transition_close.py:433`, links, audit\ncomment, compaction, push). Each is an INDEPENDENT event append with its own acquisition, so\nretrying an acquisition lands *that* event and can never replay the STATUS event. Opting\n`event_append.py` in also makes the completion-signature append survive contention, the direct\ncause of the \"closed WITHOUT a completion signature\" warning at `transition_close.py:440`.\n\n1. `acquire()` and `write_lock()` gain **`retries: int = 0`**. The default of 0 reproduces today's\n   behaviour exactly, so every caller not listed below is unchanged with no edit.\n2. **Backoff schedule (pinned):** between passes the loop sleeps `_jitter(0.5 * 2**(n-1))` for\n   pass *n*, capped at 2.0s — so ~0.5s then ~1.0s for the default 2 retries. Backoff is ADDITIVE\n   to, not carved out of, each pass's `timeout*attempts` budget. Ceiling = 3 passes x 60s + ~1.5s\n   backoff ≈ **181.5s**, the \"~180s\" figure below.\n3. Opted-in sites pass `_write_path_retries()`, reading env **`REBAR_LOCK_RETRIES`** (int, default\n   **2**, clamped `[0,10]`). `REBAR_LOCK_RETRIES=0` restores today's fail-fast.\n4. The terminating `LockTimeout` names the **cumulative** wait plus the holder; each exhausted pass\n   logs a warning naming the holder.\n5. `txn._acquire_write_lock` (`txn.py:84-86`) currently discards both by re-raising a generic\n   `CommandError(\"Error: could not acquire lock\")`. It propagates `str(exc)` instead.\n\n## Scope\n\n**Edited, opting in to retries** (exactly five call sites):\n- `src/rebar/_store/lock.py` — `retries` param, retry loop, backoff, `REBAR_LOCK_RETRIES` helper,\n  cumulative-wait message, per-pass warning.\n- `src/rebar/_store/event_append.py` — canonical write path, `write_lock()` at **382, 420, 532**.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/txn.py` — `_acquire_write_lock` (**84**), plus the message propagation.\n- `src/rebar/_store/push.py` — **664** (locked commit-and-push) opts in; **375** (advisory merge)\n  stays fail-fast.\n- `tests/unit/test_lock_retry_zebrafish.py` (new); `docs/concurrency.md`.\n\n**Deliberately NOT edited — every other caller keeps fail-fast via the `retries=0` default:**\n`compact_txn.py:340`, `compact_rebuild.py:126` (retries would undo 7084's R3 stand-aside and\nre-create the 48s holder that caused this bug); `fsck_repair.py:241`, `s3_doctor.py:199`\n(operator-driven repair); `inbound_translate.py:283` (retried at its advisory-lock layer);\n`sync.py:255`, `push.py:375`, `ensures.py:158` (best-effort sweeps).\n\n## Testing\n\n- **Happy path:** an uncontended `acquire(retries=2)` wins on the first pass and never sleeps.\n- **Reproduction (RED→GREEN):** a real subprocess holder held past one budget. With `retries=0` the\n  waiter raises `LockTimeout` (today's loss); with `retries=2` it acquires on a later pass and its\n  write is present. Scaled to seconds.\n- **No double-append:** after a contended acquire succeeding on a later pass, exactly ONE event is\n  appended — the retry never replays the caller's write body.\n- **Exhaustion:** a holder outliving all passes raises `LockTimeout` with the cumulative wait.\n- **Claim path:** a claim-shaped acquire behind an over-budget holder succeeds on a later pass; its\n  `CommandError` text carries the cumulative wait and the holder.\n- **Fail-fast preserved:** the advisory `push.py:375` merge path acquires with `retries=0`.\n- **Env override:** `REBAR_LOCK_RETRIES=0` restores single-budget fail-fast; out-of-range clamps.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Re-measured post-R1/R3/R5 main and recorded whether writes are still lost — done, numbers in\n      the AC#1 comment.\n- [ ] The failure-shape decision (retry-with-backoff over fair queueing) is recorded in Approach\n      with the evidence selecting it.\n- [ ] A write whose first budget expires is re-attempted rather than discarded, verified by\n      `pytest -q tests/unit/test_lock_retry_zebrafish.py -k reproduction` exiting 0.\n- [ ] The retry never replays the caller's write body, verified by the no-double-append test\n      asserting an appended-event count of exactly 1.\n- [ ] A write exhausting every pass raises `LockTimeout` naming the cumulative wait, verified by\n      the exhaustion test asserting the message text.\n- [ ] `claim` succeeds on a later pass behind an over-budget holder, verified by the claim-path\n      test exiting 0.\n- [ ] `claim`'s error text carries the cumulative wait, verified by asserting the `CommandError`\n      message contains it.\n- [ ] `claim`'s error text names the holder, verified by asserting the `CommandError` message\n      contains the holder string.\n- [ ] Opted-in call sites are exactly five, distributed 3/1/1, verified by\n      `diff <(grep -rln 'retries=_write_path_retries()' src/rebar --include='*.py' | xargs -n1 sh -c 'echo \"$(basename $0) $(grep -c retries=_write_path_retries $0)\"' | sort) <(printf 'event_append.py 3\\npush.py 1\\ntxn.py 1\\n')`\n- [ ] The advisory `push.py:375` merge stays fail-fast, verified by the fail-fast test asserting\n      that acquire is called with `retries=0` on that path.\n- [ ] The `retries` default is 0 so unedited callers are unchanged, verified by a test asserting\n      `inspect.signature(lock.acquire).parameters['retries'].default == 0`.\n- [ ] `REBAR_LOCK_RETRIES=0` restores single-budget fail-fast, verified by the env-override test.\n- [ ] Out-of-range `REBAR_LOCK_RETRIES` clamps to `[0,10]`, verified by the clamp test.\n- [ ] `docs/concurrency.md` documents the ~180s ceiling, verified by\n      `test \"$(grep -c '180' docs/concurrency.md)\" -ge 1`.\n- [ ] `docs/concurrency.md` documents the override, verified by\n      `test \"$(grep -c 'REBAR_LOCK_RETRIES' docs/concurrency.md)\" -ge 1`.\n- [ ] `make lint` exits 0.\n- [ ] `make typecheck` exits 0.\n- [ ] `tests/integration/test_store_concurrency.py` passes unchanged.\n- [ ] `src/rebar/_store/lock.py` stays under the 800-line cap, verified by\n      `test \"$(wc -l < src/rebar/_store/lock.py)\" -lt 800`."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786524189908564001,"uuid":"f9a41458-4b54-4647-bb43-7d703fd98fbb"}